The hypothesis on $p_0, p_i$ and~\Cref{thm:properties_exp} assure that the operator $\mathrm{d}\pa{\exp^{-1}_{p_0} \circ \exp_{p_i}}_{v_{i,k}}$ exists and is an isomorphism of linear spaces. By the chain rule, letting $w_{i,k} \coloneqq \exp^{-1}_{p_0}(x_t)$ we have that
        \[
            \mathrm{d} \pa{f \circ \exp_{p_i}}_{v_{i,k}} = \mathrm{d} \pa{f \circ \exp_{p_0}}_{w_{i,k}} \circ \mathrm{d} \pa{\exp_{p_0}^{-1} \circ \exp_{p_i}}_{v_{i,k}}
        \]
        and taking adjoints
        \begin{align*}
            \nabla\pa{f &\circ \exp_{p_i}}(v_{i,k}) =\\
            &\mathrm{d}\pa{\exp_{p_0}^{-1} \circ \exp_{p_i}}^\ast_{v_{i,k}}\pa{\nabla \pa{f \circ \exp_{p_0}}\pa{w_{i,k}}}.\qedhere
        \end{align*}
